+### Display-only Session relationships
+
+A client plugin may add creator relationships to the **native** grouped Workspace list through `ctx.uiWorkspace.sessionRelationsVersion === 1` and `registerSessionRelations({ id, version: 1, source })`. Register inside `ctx.effect` and return the supplied disposer. `source` is a `HostObservable<SessionRelationsSnapshot>`: `getSnapshot()` returns a stable readonly `{ schemaVersion: 1, edges, loading, truncated }`; `subscribe(listener)` returns cleanup. Each edge is `{ workspaceId, sourceId, targetId, kind: 'created-session' }` with the corresponding branded ids. The public types are exported from this package's client entry. No provider means the original list; no additional requests are made by this package. Providers are subscribed only while the native browser observes the aggregate, and disposal removes their edges and subscriptions.
+
+Relationships change only `displayParentId` in the row projection: they never change Session headers, `parentSession`, runtime ownership, Workspace membership, or the saved native ordering. Both endpoints must currently be ordinary roots in the same uniquely owning Workspace; missing Sessions, forks, subagent-origin Sessions, duplicate children, cross-Workspace edges, and cycles are omitted. Earlier accepted edges win parent conflicts. Hidden or archived endpoints detach their visible children into native root rows, including in Show archived mode. Flat and search lists stay flat. Grouped rows retain native selection, leading status/extension seats, hover cards, menus, actions, rename, and drag handling.
+
+A related component is admitted in full whenever any of its rows meets the native Workspace watermark. Its visible root stays at depth zero; all descendants appear at one shared depth beneath it, preserving depth-first order and leaving the original edges intact. Only the root has a collapse button, always visible immediately after its title and before the native trailing status/actions. Its browser-persisted preference is keyed by Workspace and Session, defaults to expanded, and hides the whole component without counting descendants as watermark overflow. Older child collapse preferences are ignored while those rows are descendants. Ordinary navigation, including search-result navigation and late provider arrival, reveals only the target's visible root without rewriting child preferences. Unrelated rows keep native limits and order. Roots retain the ordinary Session title start without an empty relationship gutter. Descendants reserve an independent flex gutter despite row-padding or leading-seat styling; their connectors form one vertical run with a rounded short elbow only at the final row. Loading or truncated provider snapshots produce localized informational text without replacing the native list.
+
 ### Search
 
 Collapsed search is one header action beside the view and add actions: activating it expands the field across the header. A non-blank query replaces either browsing mode with one flat result list — case-insensitive title and Workspace substring matches appear immediately, while a 250 ms debounced Host request adds ranked current-conversation content matches and snippets. Each new query aborts the preceding request; a failed content search leaves metadata matches visible without an additional warning. The list is capped at 20. Choosing an unarchived result clears and collapses search, opens the Session, and scrolls its row into view in the configured browsing mode; grouped browsing also expands its Workspace and the full Session list when required. Archived results offer Unarchive; attempting to open one explains that restriction without clearing the query or navigating.
