+
+### Server-planned group archiving
+
+The shared menu, hover action, and keyboard archive entry use `archiveSessionWithOutcome`; the existing public `archiveSession` remains a singleton operation. Providers require `ctx.uiWorkspace.sessionArchiveProvidersVersion === 2` and `registerSessionArchiveProvider({ id, version: 2, prepare, commit })`; legacy version 1 registrations are rejected. Register within `ctx.effect` and return the disposer. The public `SessionArchiveProvider`, `SessionArchiveScope`, `SessionArchiveScopeChoice`, `SessionArchivePlan`, `SessionArchiveActivity`, `SessionArchiveCommitOutcome`, and `SessionArchiveOutcome` are type-only exports. `prepare(sessionId)` returns `undefined` only when unhandled; otherwise it returns a scope question or authoritative plan. This package never derives archive scope from relationship display edges or visible rows. Planning errors surface without singleton fallback.
+
+A scope question is `{ kind: 'scope-choice', targetId, allowedScopes: ['single', 'related'] }`, with no plan id or members. The native dialog asks Only this session or All related sessions before preparing either range. Selecting calls `prepare(sessionId, { archiveScope })` afresh through the exact registered provider. `single` must be independently planned with only the target, never by filtering a related plan or consulting descendants; the provider owns that server boundary. Quiet single scope commits immediately after selection and retains single-Session undo, including for the currently viewed Session. Related scope always lists the actual complete members and asks for a second confirmation, even when quiet. Scope selection never implies stop consent.
+
+A plan names its required `archiveScope`, `planId`, `targetId`, complete `total`, `targets`, per-Session `activity`, and activity-only `requiresConfirmation`. Activity preserves nullable item ids/labels and total counts as a display DTO, not Host identities. The dialog shows exact member ids/titles and per-Session activity; active plans require a separate initially unchecked stop consent. Quiet related confirmation sends `stopActivity: false`. Cancel submits no commit. Questions and plans bind exact identity, contents, target, provider and navigation revision; changed, cancelled, consumed, unloaded or navigation-superseded requests fail closed, including late preparation. The provider receives `commit(plan, { archiveScope: plan.archiveScope, stopActivity })` once. Initial `stopActivity: true` bypasses neither scope choice nor member/stop confirmation. Server authorization, freshness, idempotency and execution remain provider-owned.
+
+Group outcomes report `succeeded`, `partial`, `unknown`, or `failed`, with confirmed `archivedIds`, `remaining`, `failed`, and `stopActivityRequested`. Confirmed archived descendants clear a matching current selection, including on partial outcomes; unrelated newer selection is preserved. Success and incomplete notices distinguish newly archived Sessions from pre-existing archive skips using the plan flags and confirmed result ids; they never offer a misleading single-root undo. Partial, uncertain and failed outcomes remain visible with counts; no automatic retry is performed. Stop-request wording does not promise that all activity stopped. The original singleton activity dialog, undo and archive filter behavior remain available when no provider handles the target.
 
 Session update times use the tertiary label color, including on archived rows. A Session title wider than its row is clipped with an ellipsis at rest. Hovering the row scrolls the title to its far edge — the incremented title of a fork, for example — and reveals it without the ellipsis; leaving the row returns the title to its start.
 
